{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5","id":1279421,"title":"Boundaries and restrictions on the Spheres at level 5.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-08T01:41:10-08:00","id":1279421,"title":"Boundaries and restrictions on the Spheres at level 5.","content":"Sorry, couldn't find a suitable title.<br /> <br /> If a Mage has 5 in all Spheres, what can't they do magick wise? I know that it's dependant on the characters paradigm, avatar essence, vulgar vs coincidental etc. but just in terms of raw power, I could use an example list of things this mage couldn't do.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:10:04-08:00","id":1279493,"title":"","content":"Questions I have first:<br /> -Do you care about the # of successes?<br /> -Do you consider Masters of the Art a book you plan on using?<br /> -Is it just the outcome you care about or the metaphysics too?<br /> <br /> There are certain classes of effects that seem to largely be outside the ken of magic or maybe are just too darn hard:<br /> -Manipulation of avatars beyond simple destruction. There's no mention of, for instance, being able to swap avatars with someone, reverse someone who's wilderslainte<br /> -Reversing the curse of Caine. I think the line is &quot;you need to get more successes than god&quot;<br /> -Changing certain high potency attributes like granting someone Fist of God, Dark Fate, True Faith, or changing someone's Destiny background<br /> -Metamagic also has no mention for instance an effect that transmutes paradigms, allows for fundamental manipulation of paradox such as granting it to someone, or changing someone's resonance or degree of Jhor taint<br /> <br /> Some of these questions get messy as for instance, reversing the curse of Caine may or may not have a rote or the Storyteller could rule that it's impossible in their universe's metaphysics. Additionally, even if you can't affect someone's resonance, you can certainly make it look like it's changed.<br /> <br /> There are certain things that'd be magically precluded, affecting an incarna or celestine or doing acts in areas where magic is barred by the physics of the realm like no magic working in the null zone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T10:50:11-08:00","id":1279502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1279493#post1279493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Metamagic also has no mention for instance an effect that transmutes paradigms,</div> </div> </div> </div>Metamagic in the sense of &quot;altering how magick works&quot; it's usually impossible or very hard. I.E: to increase the power or reach of an existing curse you would have to cast a bigger one, you can't cast more than one effect per turn w/o outside help (like with Talismans), you can't magically raise your Arete dicepool, etc...<br /> <br /> ...but changing Paradigms it's very possible. M20 has it explicitly mentioned as an Entropy 5 effect (it's in the section about eroding Belief), but, really, the most famous Paradigm-changing effect would be the Traditionalist to Technocrat conversion trough Social Conditioning. The process was intended to allow Deviants to accept a more &quot;propper&quot; Focus for their new loyalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-08-2019, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:31:12-08:00","id":1279515,"title":"","content":"I think you want to know the same as I did in this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/789697-things-mages-can-t-do\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/789697-things-mages-can-t-do\"> Things Mages can't do - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/789697-things-mages-can-t-do\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/789697-things-mages-can-t-do </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Since mages can do pratically anything, I was trying to think effects that they just can't. Maybe there aren't any, and this thread will discuss if this is tru or not. First effect that I believe mages cannot do is increase spheres or Arete using magick. I believe that is more a balancing thing than anything, otherwise any mage with Mind(maybe spirit) would have a lot more Arete or sphere points for free, even if temporarily. Another one is immortality. I know mages with Life can extend they lifespan greately (this makes me wonder for how long it is possible, and hhow would this be ruled..?) and maybe </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:36:12-08:00","id":1279537,"title":"","content":"Even assuming infinite successes, there are a few things that should remain out of bounds just for sanity's sake. A Mage can't target the consensus itself, for instance. She might be able to mass mind control everyone in an area, but it is not clear how quickly something like that would change the local consensus. Raising Arete should also also be It's also a really good idea to assume that a Mage cannot change morality (many might fall into the trap of thinking Might Makes Right, but we should never confirm if they are correct). <br /> <br /> Certain things should also be what I call Ascension Level tasks, that is they are equivalent to achieving Mass Ascension and they should be handled as such. Altering the Curse of Caine itself so that there is a static cure, creating an anti-Caul that repairs inverted Avatars, or fundamentally changing an unstatted being like a Celestine or Neverborn would be good examples. They might theoretically possible for a Master but they involve substantially more than just casting a single infinite success spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T13:23:21-08:00","id":1279553,"title":"","content":"As a note, I like the idea of the 10th sphere being attempts to fill in these spots of impossible. My players are currently dealing with an entity that blew itself into 3 copies of itself, each with access to only 3 spheres during a backlash attempting to manipulate the avatar of someone who was minimally conscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T22:39:21-08:00","id":1279647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1279493#post1279493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Manipulation of avatars beyond simple destruction. There's no mention of, for instance, being able to swap avatars with someone, reverse someone who's wilderslainte<br /> -Reversing the curse of Caine. I think the line is &quot;you need to get more successes than god&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The focus character for the Euthanatos was a former wilderslainte.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for whether one can remove the Curse of Caine.. one book says &quot;can you roll more succcesses than God&quot; another basically says &quot;Sure now lets see what happen&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T03:40:58-08:00","id":1279668,"title":"","content":"A lot of the things mentionned here as impossible for mages were, ironically, done or understated to be achievable in one book or another.<br /> <br /> The curse of Caine for exemple, never in any fictive universe have I seen an impossible thing achieved so many times!<br /> <br /> The red sign, to begin with, is all about mages and vampires reversing it.<br /> <br /> The novel House of secret is all about a tremere project to escape vampirism with the help of a few mages cabals, and nearly achieving such escape.<br /> <br /> (And there is a character in the novel that do so and become a mage anew).<br /> <br /> And we have a character in the Ascension warrior trilogy which is &quot;one of those that can bring back a vampire to life&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Metamagic in the sense of &quot;altering how magick works&quot; it's usually impossible or very hard. &quot;<br /> <br /> I know it's not a very known book, but the mage chapter of &quot;world of darkness :France&quot; has a set of rules for metamagic.<br /> <br /> &quot;Manipulation of avatars beyond simple destruction.<br /> Master of the art allows spirit archmasters to manipulate avatars.<br /> <br /> The well of Soul(infinite tapestry) allows to change one's avatar essence.<br /> <br /> &quot;There's no mention of, for instance, being able to swap avatars with someone&quot;<br /> <br /> The infinite tapestry ( and maybe also the book of world) speak of the shade realm of Spirit, where your avatar manifest and can be lost, it clearly mention that you can use this place to take another's avatar for yourself if you lost your own.<br /> <br /> &quot;reverse someone who's wilderslainte'&quot;<br /> <br /> If my memory serves, there's this description of the Flux in book of world &quot;<br /> A nephandi craving redemption, potentially after multiple lives, could purge himself of dark ess in the heart of this Realm&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T06:18:52-08:00","id":1279684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1279668#post1279668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the things mentionned here as impossible for mages were, ironically, done or understated to be achievable in one book or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's true, however this thread it's about what a mage can't do no matter how many Spheres he has at 5, it's about what &quot;ordinary magick&quot; can't do...<br /> <br /> That's why stuff like manipulating Paradox beyond simple reduction it's mentioned, in spite of the fact Prime Archmasters can explicitly do so.<br /> <br /> I believe that, for mages, &quot;totally impossible&quot; just means &quot;maybe I'm going to have to leave the Sanctum and work my elbows for this one&quot;...but that's not to say that there aren't things beyond having 9 Spheres at 5 and a bucket of Arete dice - and that's the intended purpose of this thread.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The curse of Caine for exemple, never in any fictive universe have I seen an impossible thing achieved so many times! </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Curse can explicitly be cured with True Magick and has been done in canon more than once....but not as a function of having Spheres at 5.<br /> <br /> It's not what we could call &quot;ordinary magick&quot;, in one book it's a function of Archmagick, in other it's a quest that includes a mckguffin that makes the feat more reachable.<br /> Not just anyone reverses the Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know it's not a very known book, but the mage chapter of &quot;world of darkness :France&quot; has a set of rules for metamagic. </div> </div> </div>Gota check it. That's very interesting data albeit very &quot;out there&quot;. Does it allow to alter magick <i>with Sphere Magick</i>?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Manipulation of avatars beyond simple destruction.<br /> Master of the art allows spirit archmasters to manipulate avatars. </div> </div> </div>Archmasters can awaken avatars with Arch-Spirit 9 and violate their Quintessence with Prime 7. Both way beyond ordinary magick. Other than that the only thing mentioned in that book it's about &quot;skinning&quot; your Avatar to shred Permadox...which it's kinda like destroying it, just slower. MotA also implies it's an one way road, there's no simple way to repair the Avatar mentioned there. If Avatar manipulation was easily doable there would be a method to &quot;heal&quot; such damage mentioned there, but it isn't.<br /> <br /> That being said a certain degree of manipulation seems possible. In BoS you can create Phylacteries, which means you can &quot;tie&quot; avatars to other stuff.<br /> <br /> Ascencion describes the (granted, not 100% canon) Rote that Heyel invented to fuse two persons with their Avatars and it's not beyond 5 (it just needs a rare kind of lore most people do not posess). The Matriarch also was made of fused mages, albeit we do not know if they weren't sharing one Avatar already.<br /> <br /> Avatar manipulation sure it's rare but all things considered maybe, <i>maybe</i>, basic Avatar manipulation isn't *that* hard.<br /> <br /> Now, Avatar <i>transmutation</i> or Avatar <i>creation </i>on the other hand...THAT'S Hard with major H. The first one seems to require the intervention of potent Umbrood or Realms, while the second has never been done (as far as I know, it may be the province of God or the Psychopomps alone)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The well of Soul(infinite tapestry) allows to change one's avatar essence. </div> </div> </div>That's not Sphere Magick, but a property of a Realm of extraordinary power (think that this realm was one of the few Astral Realms that survived the Avatar Storm almost unscratched) And not just any Realm, but one that's implied to be related with Avatars and their reincarnation cycle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;There's no mention of, for instance, being able to swap avatars with someone&quot;<br /> <br /> The infinite tapestry ( and maybe also the book of world) speak of the shade realm of Spirit, where your avatar manifest and can be lost, it clearly mention that you can use this place to take another's avatar for yourself if you lost your own. </div> </div> </div>Another good example of something that ordinary magic can't do, since you needed to go all the way to the Deep Umbra (which by itself requires Spirit 5) to achieve it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;reverse someone who's wilderslainte'&quot;<br /> <br /> If my memory serves, there's this description of the Flux in book of world &quot;<br /> A nephandi craving redemption, potentially after multiple lives, could purge himself of dark ess in the heart of this Realm&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, regardless of your memory the Flux can do things Spheres at 5 can't. Like removing Permadox for instance. And finding a Nephandi that craves redemption would be a legendary circumstance all by itself<br /> <br /> Probably the best known case of reversed wildderslainte it's Senex Apprentice. But with Senex there combined with the cautionary tales about them one can't be sure if this isn't a function of Senex having Spheres above 5 (or having some other esoterical resource beyond ordinary magick). <hr /><br /> Having said that, the thing with the limits of Spheres at 5 it's that they depend a lot on ST fiat.<br /> <br /> I think that a good bottom line about all of this it's that<i> the limits are in no way clear.</i> Altrough some feats do have a big &quot;NO&quot; sign at the door (i.e reversing Nephandism/Marauderdoom) nobody knows if this is &quot;impossible with normal magick&quot; or just a little harder than most mages ever tried.<br /> <br /> So, a lot of the things mentioned here <i>might</i> be doable...if the ST allows. The things mentioned here are stuff that was either restricted somewhere or that were never allowed trough simple spellcasting (and could break the game if allowed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-09-2019, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T06:26:06-08:00","id":1279687,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the question was about what you could do with a 5 in all spheres, not what you could do with Archmastery or special locations. That's why I didn't bring up Senex healing an inverted Avatar, because we don't know how he did it. It is entirely possible he just kept killing its reincarnations until it healed itself. That is a canonical way of doing it, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T07:28:22-08:00","id":1279692,"title":"","content":"I think it gets down to a Master Mage is more capable of making use of various magguffins either by having better access to Umbrood, travel, etc. IF we assume infinite resources along with infinite successes then.. probably anything?<br /> <br /> The Issue is always resources. Its not just a matter of quint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T05:51:33-08:00","id":1280084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1279493#post1279493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Reversing the curse of Caine. I think the line is &quot;you need to get more successes than god&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is</i> the ritual of the Red Sign, but that &quot;cheats&quot; by summoning a Psychopomp to do the heavy lifting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T07:05:40-08:00","id":1280098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1279687#post1279687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is entirely possible he just kept killing its reincarnations until it healed itself. That is a canonical way of doing it, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin of the well-known Euthanatoic phrase: Spare the mage, spoil the avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T12:38:23-08:00","id":1280157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1280084#post1280084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There <i>is</i> the ritual of the Red Sign, but that &quot;cheats&quot; by summoning a Psychopomp to do the heavy lifting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not really cheating if its how its done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T13:32:50-08:00","id":1280171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1280157#post1280157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its not really cheating if its how its done.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it's a cheat in that I feel the OP was implicitly &quot;how to do it with spheres alone&quot;. All of these are obviated by &quot;get a celestine or incarna to do it for you&quot; and I feel this kind of fits into that bucket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T14:33:06-08:00","id":1280178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1280171#post1280171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it's a cheat in that I feel the OP was implicitly &quot;how to do it with spheres alone&quot;. All of these are obviated by &quot;get a celestine or incarna to do it for you&quot; and I feel this kind of fits into that bucket.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's very few things that can be done with &quot;sphere's alone&quot; Primum for example requires a vast array of particular resources and can't just be say conjured in a lab. That spheres can bring in the assistance of powerful entities is an option. That spheres can allow a character to engage with entities that can do their work for them is an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T15:55:17-08:00","id":1280196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279421-boundaries-and-restrictions-on-the-spheres-at-level-5?p=1280178#post1280178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's very few things that can be done with &quot;sphere's alone&quot; Primum for example requires a vast array of particular resources and can't just be say conjured in a lab.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true.<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0 The requeriments on Primium are explicitly dependant on Paradigm as the method AND resources employed by Iteration X it's not the same as the one employed by the Childrens of Knowledge and thus presumably other methods that require less or no base materials could be invented.<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0 None of the resources employed by Primium can't be conjured. You can conjure gold and the other requires props. You can conjure a lab complete with it's own energy. You can even conjure the Tass with enough Prime.<br /> <br /> You do need &quot;special knowledge&quot;, though. After all it's supposed to be a trade secret.<br /> But if you have that you can totally summon the rest out of thin air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That spheres can bring in the assistance of powerful entities is an option. That spheres can allow a character to engage with entities that can do their work for them is an option. </div> </div> </div>If &quot;anything&quot; external counts as resource then you do not need Spheres to do anything. Just have God do it for ya.<br /> <br /> That's why that aproach it's &quot;cheating&quot;. You're not really talking about what the Spheres can do, you're merely giving examples where Spheres were tangentially employed.<br /> <br /> *Let me give you a clear example of WHY:<br /> <br /> &quot;How can I provoque a nuclear explosion?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Forces 3, perhaps even 2, can cause nuclear explosions&quot;. This is totally true: Forces 3 can manipulate electronic media and machines, and thus if I just happen to be near a nuclear misile, I could program it to detonate right there (it would require a rare set of circumstances, like having a nuclear misile ready to launch, being near the launching controls but, hey, Forces could help to bypass so many security measures and the rest are &quot;resources&quot;...).<br /> <br /> But you know very well that the level to summon nuclear explosions it's 5, don't you?...<br /> <br /> See.<br /> <br /> The question it's about what can't be done &quot;with All Spheres at 5&quot;. Since everything and anything can be done with infinite resources alone regardless of magick (I could always have the unconditional help of God or infinite Talismans as &quot;resources&quot; in that case) that's no way of answering the question,<br /> <br /> So, let's cut the rhetoric right now, shall we:<br /> The question it's about <i>&quot;das Rules&quot;</i> not some obscure philosophical question about what constitutes Spheres in a Vacuum.<br /> <br /> A modicum amount of resources are to be expected: Like, say &quot;having an Avatar&quot;, &quot;having a Focus/Paradigm&quot;(this one was mentioned by the OP) and presumably &quot;knowing what you're doing&quot; too (since Spheres can't do anything otherwise). God and the True Cross as a resource isn't fair by any sort of <i>good faith</i> (and neither its ultra rare unique Grimoires that may not even be fabricable trough magic plus the help of a divine being).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-11-2019, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T10:41:56-08:00","id":1284757,"title":"","content":"The First Edition Corebook gives some examples of results that are not within the capabilities of Magick Effects with particular Spheres at Levels 5. In the case of the Matter and Entropy examples, it is stated that a particular result might be within the capabilities of Oracles.<br /> Matter \u2013 Creation of Matter-based entities.<br /> Entropy \u2013 Affecting ideas on level of societies. Making a person forget who she ( or he ) is.<br /> Mind \u2013 Pure mental existence. There is an allusion to \u201chigher powers\u201d that Oracles might have.<br /> <br /> The levels 6-9 of Archspheres in the \u201c<i>Masters of the Art</i>\u201d book should give some ideas in regard to limits and boundaries of Magickal Effects. Also, I think a that careful and throughout reading and consideration of the capabilities of the Spheres should reveal some limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-04-2019, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T09:13:24-08:00","id":1284976,"title":"","content":"They can't create EXP.<br /> <br /> For me, Archspheres should be the following:<br /> <br /> - Archmastery should be clearly described a trap out-of-universe, but seen as the pinnacle of achievement in-universe. Archmastery is losing sight of ascension and instead doubling down on More Power.<br /> <br /> - Archmastery should be represented by a level 6 power which simply fills in a bunch of gaps left by the previous levels. With level 6 spirit you are creating Avatars, splitting them into pieces, redeeming lost souls, healing a &quot;dead&quot; soul that it can truly return to a normal life with the right host... none of this is easy. It demands powerful tools and the right input. An Archmage NPC should be saying &quot;I need you to bring me X&quot; rather than &quot;I'll have that done in 5 minutes&quot;. That way even if they're your unconditional ally the game keeps some sense of balance. Yeah your friend can remove Permanent Paradox but to do it he needs to cut away a bit of your Avatar. And your friend can increase your Avatar's power, but you need to provide him with an absurd amount of Quintessence of a spare Avatar he can work with, and there are loads of practical and moral implications associated with all of this.<br /> <br /> - Archmages should only realize their mistake (if they ever do) when it's too late, and become partly consumed by their own craft. They stop being active agents in the world and become more like powerful spirits. They're not the protagonist by any means, they're a part of other people's stories. Their work consumes so much of their attention that they rarely leave the place where they work, if ever. They're a potential source of paradox free time travel, but they're opening the door for you and letting you get on with your adventure. They would never come along and make sure you get home safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-05-2019, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}